    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are analyzing a LinkedIn post to extract reusable content patterns — not to summarize what it says. Do not repeat the post's specific facts, names, numbers, or claims in your output.\n\nExtract the following from the text below:\n1. hook_type — how the first line grabs attention (question, bold claim, statistic, contrarian statement, story-open, curiosity-gap, etc.)\n2. structure — the overall shape of the post (problem→solution, numbered list, before/after, narrative arc, listicle, single-insight, etc.)\n3. tone — the overall voice (educational, provocative, personal/vulnerable, technical, humorous, etc.)\n4. formatting_notes — how it's visually formatted (line break frequency, emoji use, bullet/numbering use, approximate length, paragraph structure)\n5. cta_type — what kind of call-to-action is used, if any (question to audience, soft ask, link-in-comments, direct link, none)\n6. anti_patterns — anything in this post that likely hurt engagement (generic opener, no CTA, wall of text, overused hashtag pattern, buried hook, etc.) — return an empty list if none are apparent\n\nText to analyze:\n{{ $json.text }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
